hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: ""When you say to your companion on the day of Jumu'ah, 'Be quiet,' while the Imam is delivering the sermon, then you have engaged in idle talk."""
"19","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""When you say to your companion on the day of Jumu'ah, 'Be quiet,' while the Imam is delivering the sermon, then you have engaged in idle talk."""
"20","Abdullah bin Ibrahim Zahri narrated, he saw Hazrat Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) performing ablution on the roof of the mosque, so Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I performed ablution because I ate a piece of cheese, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying, ""Perform ablution after eating something cooked on fire."""
"21","Abd bin Ibrahim Zahri (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated, I saw Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) performing ablution on top of the mosque, so he was asked: Do you know why I am performing ablution? I have eaten pieces of cheese, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Perform ablution after eating something cooked on fire."" Imam Zahri (may Allah have mercy on him) used to perform ablution after eating something cooked on fire."
"22","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Qariz that he found Hazrat Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) performing ablution on the roof of the mosque. Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I am performing ablution because I have eaten pieces of cheese. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform ablution after eating something cooked on fire."""
"23","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying, ""On the day of Jumu'ah, when you say to your companion 'Be quiet' while the Imam is delivering the sermon, then you have engaged in idle talk."""
"24","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Ibrahim Zahri that he saw Hazrat Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) performing ablution on the roof of the mosque, so he asked him, ""With what are you performing ablution?"" Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) replied, ""Do you not know why I am performing ablution? I am performing ablution because I ate a piece of cheese, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Perform ablution after eating something cooked on fire.'"""
"25","Abdullah bin Ibrahim bin Qariz Zahri narrated: I saw Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) performing ablution on the roof of the mosque, when he had eaten pieces of cheese, so he performed ablution. I asked: Do you perform ablution after eating cheese? He replied: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) saying, ""Perform ablution after eating anything cooked on fire."""
"26","Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Qariz narrated: I heard Sayyiduna Muawiyah bin Abu Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with them) saying from the pulpit in Madinah Tayyibah: ""O people of Madinah, where are your jurists? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbidding doing the hair in this manner near the pulpit."" Then he placed a wig on his hair and demonstrated. I have not seen anyone, on the occasion of a wedding or otherwise, with hair as beautiful as that of Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him). Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""May Allah curse the woman who tattoos and the one who gets tattooed, the one who plucks facial hair (makes eyebrows) and the one who gets them plucked (has her eyebrows made), and the one who files teeth and the one who gets them filed."""
